        "original_id": "cba1a479-0a1d-578a-95d5-36df85d43bd3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Summerseat, Greater Manchester, England, north west England, Heywood, Rawtenstall, Bury Bolton Street, Burrs Country Park, Ramsbottom, Irwell Vale\n- Organizations: East Lancashire Railway\n- Stations: Summerseat railway station, Broadfield railway station\n- Systems: heritage railways, preserved railway stations\n\nFacts:\n- The East Lancashire Railway is a heritage railway line in north west England that runs between Heywood and Rawtenstall.\n- The East Lancashire Railway is about 12 to 12.5 miles long and has intermediate stations at Bury Bolton Street, Burrs Country Park, Summerseat, Ramsbottom, and Irwell Vale.\n- Summerseat railway station is a preserved railway station serving the village of Summerseat in Greater Manchester, England.\n- Summerseat railway station is part of the heritage East Lancashire Railway.\n- The line through Broadfield railway station has been reopened by the heritage East Lancashire Railway.\n- Broadfield railway station itself remains disused.",
